# Explorer 3 Technical Report: Modernized Full-Bleed Detail View Overlay & Cast Chips

**Milestone**: UI-M2  
**Target Platform**: LG 32LR686BPSA (1920x1080 Full HD, webOS 8.5.0, Chromium ~108 WAM)  
**Assigned Directory**: `/home/prem/webos-projects/cinejoy-webos/.agents/teamwork/explorer_ui_m2_3/`  
**Date**: 2026-11-05  

---

## 1. Executive Summary

This investigation designs the modernized Google TV / cinema-grade **Detail View Overlay** for the CineJoy LG webOS application (`com.cinejoy.tv`), based on the reference patterns in `.tmp_ref/theboringtv-lgwebos/features/details.*`.

The redesigned Detail View transforms the existing 520px hero section into an immersive, full-bleed cinematic overlay featuring:
1. **Full-Bleed Backdrop Art with Dual-Gradient Scrim (`.dshade`)**: Dark cinema canvas (`#0e1014`) crossfading through a dual-gradient scrim (horizontal 90° and vertical 0°) that isolates text on the left and bottom while showcasing high-resolution TMDB artwork on the right and top.
2. **Elevated Typography Hierarchy**:
   - Title scaled to 60px (56–64px spec) in semi-bold cinema typography with 24px drop-shadow.
   - Metadata chips row: rating badge (`#FACC15`), 4K UHD quality badge (`#95FF50`), release year, runtime, and genre pills.
   - Synopsis overview (`#details-overview`, `.dsub`): 24px readable typography with 3-line clamp (`max-height: 108px`).
3. **Sleek Cast & Crew Pill Chips**:
   - Modernized from vertical cards into sleek Google TV horizontal pill chips with 44px circular avatar thumbnails, `#e8eaed` actor names, and `#9aa0a6` character roles separated by mid-dots (`·`).
4. **Floating Action Pill Buttons (`.dbtn`)**:
   - Primary Play button (`#details-play-btn`) in solid white surface (`#FFFFFF`) with inverted text (`#202124`), transitioning on remote D-pad focus to electric neon lime (`#95FF50`) with a 5px pure-white halo ring and 28px glow elevation.
   - Secondary Trailer (`#details-trailer-btn`) and Back (`#details-back-btn`) pills in translucent glass (`rgba(232, 234, 237, 0.16)`), elevating on focus to pure white with inverted text.
5. **Seasons & Episodes Carousel**:
   - 16:9 episode still cards (`320px × 180px`) with 14px border radius on `#26292f` card surfaces, episode badge (`E1`), runtime pill, and high-contrast focus scaling (`scale(1.08)` + 5px white halo).
6. **Zero DOM Sinks & Invariant Preservation**:
   - 100% elimination of `.innerHTML =` and `.outerHTML =` in `app/js/views/details.js`.
   - Preservation of all 11 invariant DOM IDs: `#details-title`, `#details-meta-rating`, `#details-meta-year`, `#details-meta-runtime`, `#details-meta-quality`, `#details-overview`, `#details-play-btn`, `#details-season-selector`, `#details-episodes-shelf`, `#details-cast-shelf`, `#details-backdrop-img`.
   - Complete preservation of spatial D-pad navigation, focus memory, and remote Back key (keycode 461 / 27) returning to the origin view.

---

## 2. Reference Design Token & Pattern Integration

### 2.1 Pattern Comparison: `theboringtv` vs CineJoy Current vs CineJoy Proposed

| Component / Token | `.tmp_ref/theboringtv-lgwebos` | CineJoy Current (`app/`) | CineJoy Proposed Modernization |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Canvas Background** | `#0e1014` | `#04120B` | `#0e1014` (`--cinema-bg-base`) |
| **Backdrop Scrim** | `.dshade` dual gradient (90° & 0°) | `.details-gradient-overlay` (linear) | `.dshade` / `.details-gradient-overlay` dual gradient |
| **Title Typography** | `h1` 64px, 500 weight, 1.06 line-height | `.details-title` 40px (h1) | `.details-title` 60px, 600 weight, 1.08 line-height |
| **Synopsis** | `.dsub` 24px `#dadce0`, 1.4 line-height | `.details-synopsis` 22px `#FFFFFF` | `#details-overview` / `.dsub` 24px `#dadce0`, 1.45 line-height |
| **Cast Layout** | `.dcast` text summary `#9aa0a6` | `.cast-item` 76px circular avatar + vertical stacked text | `.cast-item` sleek horizontal pill chips (44px avatar, `#e8eaed` name, `#9aa0a6` role) |
| **Action Buttons** | `.dbtn` 24px pill, radius 30px, `rgba(232,234,237,.16)` | `.btn` 52px pill, green primary / translucent secondary | `.dbtn` 56px pill, radius 30px, white primary / translucent secondary, 10-foot focus halos |
| **Episode Cards** | N/A (Movie focus) | `.card-episode` 320x180px, radius 8px | `.card-episode` 320x180px, 14px radius, `#26292f` surface |
| **Season Pills** | N/A | `.season-pill` green active pill | `.season-pill` Google TV pill, 30px radius, `#FFFFFF` focus |
| **DOM Sinks** | `.innerHTML =` throughout | 5 instances of `.innerHTML =` in `details.js` | **0 instances** (pure DOM APIs only) |

---

## 3. Invariant DOM IDs Audit

All 11 invariant IDs specified in the task dispatch are guaranteed:

| # | Invariant DOM ID | Current Element in `app/index.html` | Proposed Modernized Markup |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 1 | `#details-title` | `<h1 id="details-title" class="details-title">` | `<h1 id="details-title" class="details-title">` |
| 2 | `#details-meta-rating` | `<span id="details-meta-rating" class="badge-pill rating">` | `<span id="details-meta-rating" class="badge-pill rating">` |
| 3 | `#details-meta-year` | `<span id="details-meta-year" class="badge-pill">` | `<span id="details-meta-year" class="badge-pill">` |
| 4 | `#details-meta-runtime` | `<span class="badge-pill">2h 46m</span>` (no ID) | `<span id="details-meta-runtime" class="badge-pill">` |
| 5 | `#details-meta-quality` | `<span class="badge-pill accent">PG-13</span>` (no ID) | `<span id="details-meta-quality" class="badge-pill accent quality">` |
| 6 | `#details-overview` | `<p class="details-synopsis">` (no ID) | `<p id="details-overview" class="details-synopsis dsub">` |
| 7 | `#details-play-btn` | `<button id="details-play-btn" class="btn btn-primary">` | `<button id="details-play-btn" class="btn btn-primary dbtn">` |
| 8 | `#details-season-selector` | `<div class="season-selector-bar">` (no ID) | `<div id="details-season-selector" class="season-selector-bar">` |
| 9 | `#details-episodes-shelf` | `<section class="content-shelf">` (no ID) | `<section id="details-episodes-shelf" class="content-shelf">` |
| 10 | `#details-cast-shelf` | `<section class="content-shelf">` (no ID) | `<section id="details-cast-shelf" class="content-shelf">` |
| 11 | `#details-backdrop-img` | `<img class="details-backdrop-img" ...>` (no ID) | `<img id="details-backdrop-img" class="details-backdrop-img dbg" ...>` |

---

## 4. Eradication of DOM Sinks (Zero-Sink Guarantee)

Analysis of `app/js/views/details.js` revealed 5 direct `.innerHTML =` assignments:
- **Line 183**: `rail.innerHTML = '';`
- **Line 231**: `bar.innerHTML = '';`
- **Line 268**: `rail.innerHTML = '';`
- **Line 298**: `recShelf.innerHTML = '<div class="shelf-header">...'`
- **Line 317**: `rail.innerHTML = '';`

### Replacement Strategy:
1. **Container Cleansing**:
   Define `clearElement(el)` helper:
   ```javascript
   function clearElement(element) {
     if (!element) return;
     while (element.firstChild) {
       element.removeChild(element.firstChild);
     }
   }
   ```
   This replaces `el.innerHTML = ''` across lines 183, 231, 268, and 317 with high-performance, sink-free node removal.
2. **Dynamic Shelf Construction (Line 298)**:
   Instead of concatenating HTML strings, construct the recommendations shelf using pure DOM factory calls:
   ```javascript
   var headerDiv = document.createElement('div');
   headerDiv.className = 'shelf-header';
   var titleH2 = document.createElement('h2');
   titleH2.className = 'shelf-title';
   titleH2.textContent = 'More Like This';
   headerDiv.appendChild(titleH2);
   recShelf.appendChild(headerDiv);

   var railDiv = document.createElement('div');
   railDiv.id = 'details-recommendations-rail';
   railDiv.className = 'shelf-rail';
   recShelf.appendChild(railDiv);
   ```

---

## 5. Proposed Code Diffs & Specifications

### 5.1 CSS Modernization (`app/css/components.css`)

Replace lines 545–690 in `app/css/components.css` with:

